1
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:41,017
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:45,017
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,017 --> 00:02:52,017
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,017 --> 00:02:59,017
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:59,017 --> 00:03:09,017
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, set sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,017 --> 00:03:13,017
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:15,017 --> 00:03:23,017
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:23,017 --> 00:03:32,017
There, they found themselves facing the New Fishman Pirates, who were looking to destroy the Ryugu Kingdom and instigated an all-out war.

9
00:03:32,017 --> 00:03:38,017
Luffy finally defeated Hordy, the captain of the New Fishman Pirates, thwarting their plan for revenge.

10
00:03:38,017 --> 00:03:39,017
Here's the Sunny!

11
00:03:39,017 --> 00:03:40,017
Yeah!

12
00:03:40,017 --> 00:03:41,017
I see Frankie!

13
00:03:41,017 --> 00:03:43,017
He looks like he's ready to set sail!

14
00:03:43,017 --> 00:03:47,017
I can't wait!

15
00:03:47,017 --> 00:03:53,017
Finally time to go!

16
00:03:53,017 --> 00:03:55,017
Goodbye, Fishman Island!

17
00:03:55,017 --> 00:04:08,017
Madam Charlie, Luffy and his friends are setting sail now.

18
00:04:08,017 --> 00:04:10,017
Oh?

19
00:04:10,017 --> 00:04:12,017
Perhaps you should see them off?

20
00:04:12,017 --> 00:04:14,017
Sure thing!

21
00:04:14,017 --> 00:04:15,017
Wait up!

22
00:04:15,017 --> 00:04:18,017
We wanna go say goodbye too!

23
00:04:18,017 --> 00:04:19,017
Sorry.

24
00:04:19,017 --> 00:04:22,017
But I need somebody to stay here and run the cafe.

25
00:04:22,017 --> 00:04:26,017
We'll have more tourists here now that we're rid of that despicable Hordy.

26
00:04:26,017 --> 00:04:30,017
So I need you girls to keep this place in tip-top shape for me, okay?

27
00:04:30,017 --> 00:04:33,017
You got it, Madam Charlie.

28
00:04:33,017 --> 00:04:43,017
Oh, the crystal ball?

29
00:04:43,017 --> 00:04:44,017
Don't worry.

30
00:04:44,017 --> 00:04:46,017
I'm through with that now.

31
00:04:46,017 --> 00:04:49,017
I don't need to look into the future anymore.

32
00:04:49,017 --> 00:04:55,017
After all, Fishman Island being torn apart by straw hat Luffy.

33
00:04:55,017 --> 00:05:00,017
Well, that's a future I never wanted to see.

34
00:05:00,017 --> 00:05:07,017
So if my prediction turned out to be incorrect this time, then nothing would make me happier.

35
00:05:07,017 --> 00:05:09,017
She knows her visions are never wrong.

36
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:12,017
She must be more scared than anyone.

37
00:05:12,017 --> 00:05:15,017
And it may not come true anytime soon.

38
00:05:15,017 --> 00:05:19,017
It could be tomorrow, or a year from now.

39
00:05:19,017 --> 00:05:23,017
So we don't know when we can stop worrying.

40
00:05:23,017 --> 00:05:27,017
Look, Madam Charlie, I know you're afraid, but Luffy-chin and the others would never-

41
00:05:27,017 --> 00:05:29,017
Kami.

42
00:05:29,017 --> 00:05:31,017
I hope that you'll forgive me.

43
00:05:31,017 --> 00:05:33,017
I shouldn't have suspected your friends.

44
00:05:33,017 --> 00:05:35,017
I see that now.

45
00:05:35,017 --> 00:05:38,017
So you'd like me to trust the straw hat boy then?

46
00:05:38,017 --> 00:05:40,017
Um...

47
00:05:40,017 --> 00:05:42,017
Uh-huh!

48
00:05:42,017 --> 00:05:54,017
Here you go!

49
00:05:54,017 --> 00:05:55,017
For your trip!

50
00:05:55,017 --> 00:05:56,017
Swing!

51
00:05:56,017 --> 00:05:57,017
Thanks, everybody!

52
00:05:57,017 --> 00:05:58,017
You ready?

53
00:05:58,017 --> 00:05:59,017
Oh, Luffy!

54
00:05:59,017 --> 00:06:04,017
Do you really have to set sail from here immediately?

55
00:06:04,017 --> 00:06:07,017
I-I hope we just met you!

56
00:06:07,017 --> 00:06:10,017
Stay with us at least one more day!

57
00:06:10,017 --> 00:06:12,017
No, better yet, another week!

58
00:06:12,017 --> 00:06:14,017
Or a year, perhaps?

59
00:06:14,017 --> 00:06:18,017
Geez, Weepy Hochi, you haven't stopped crying since the moment we met, have you?

60
00:06:18,017 --> 00:06:19,017
You're right.

61
00:06:19,017 --> 00:06:21,017
I'm always a crybaby.

62
00:06:21,017 --> 00:06:23,017
I'm sorry, Luffy.

63
00:06:23,017 --> 00:06:24,017
Whoa!

64
00:06:24,017 --> 00:06:31,017
I can't believe my fantasy is finally coming true!

65
00:06:31,017 --> 00:06:36,017
The beautiful mermaid princess is in tears because she can't bear to see me go!

66
00:06:36,017 --> 00:06:38,017
Bye, Sanji!

67
00:06:38,017 --> 00:06:39,017
Forget the new world!

68
00:06:39,017 --> 00:06:42,017
I'm happy right here!

69
00:06:42,017 --> 00:06:44,017
I agree!

70
00:06:44,017 --> 00:06:49,017
In fact, our time with these ladies has inspired me to compose a new song!

71
00:06:49,017 --> 00:06:54,017
I met my girlfriend at the mermaid cafe!

72
00:06:54,017 --> 00:06:56,017
Try not to cry!

73
00:06:56,017 --> 00:06:59,017
I'll always have a place in my heart for every one of you!

74
00:06:59,017 --> 00:07:02,017
I like that idea.

75
00:07:02,017 --> 00:07:03,017
Maybe you should stay here.

76
00:07:03,017 --> 00:07:05,017
I don't want to watch you drown in your own nosebleeds.

77
00:07:05,017 --> 00:07:09,017
You're just jealous because they're not begging you to stay, ugly!

78
00:07:09,017 --> 00:07:11,017
Who are you calling ugly?!

79
00:07:11,017 --> 00:07:13,017
Your Majesty!

80
00:07:13,017 --> 00:07:14,017
Hmm?

81
00:07:14,017 --> 00:07:16,017
Should you tell them or should I?

82
00:07:16,017 --> 00:07:20,017
It's only a matter of time until the tomate box reaches her!

83
00:07:20,017 --> 00:07:22,017
They need to know!

84
00:07:22,017 --> 00:07:25,017
If Big Mom opens the box, it'll explode!

85
00:07:28,017 --> 00:07:31,017
Yes, but look at them!

86
00:07:35,017 --> 00:07:38,017
It's all over!

87
00:07:38,017 --> 00:07:41,017
We can't go to the new world now!

88
00:07:41,017 --> 00:07:44,017
Big Mom's gonna murder us the second we get there!

89
00:07:44,017 --> 00:07:49,017
Maybe if we start sending her every piece of treasure we find for the rest of our lives,

90
00:07:49,017 --> 00:07:52,017
she might let it slide just this way!

91
00:07:52,017 --> 00:07:57,017
If we tell them they sent her a bomb, they'll lose their will to live!

92
00:07:57,017 --> 00:08:01,017
Come to think of it, Minister of the Right, those explosives are ten years old!

93
00:08:01,017 --> 00:08:04,017
It's possible they're no longer functional!

94
00:08:04,017 --> 00:08:07,017
Oh, I admire your positivity, Your Majesty!

95
00:08:07,017 --> 00:08:10,017
We do keep it rather humid in the Ryugu Palace after all!

96
00:08:10,017 --> 00:08:13,017
And who really knows if Big Mom will open the box herself anyway!

97
00:08:13,017 --> 00:08:16,017
Right, then let's just hope for the best!

98
00:08:16,017 --> 00:08:20,017
Do I want to know what you two are whispering about?

99
00:08:22,017 --> 00:08:23,017
Hmm?

100
00:08:23,017 --> 00:08:25,017
Uh, what's this?

101
00:08:25,017 --> 00:08:28,017
It's a log pose for the new world.

102
00:08:28,017 --> 00:08:30,017
I'd like you to take it with you.

103
00:08:30,017 --> 00:08:34,017
It frightened me to think that the one you'd be using had only a single needle.

104
00:08:34,017 --> 00:08:35,017
Huh?

105
00:08:35,017 --> 00:08:36,017
What's up, Nami?

106
00:08:36,017 --> 00:08:38,017
So you got a new log pose?

107
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:39,017
Whoa!

108
00:08:39,017 --> 00:08:41,017
It looks pretty cool!

109
00:08:41,017 --> 00:08:45,017
But why does it have three needles?

110
00:08:45,017 --> 00:08:48,017
Well, take a look at the log pose on your wrist.

111
00:08:48,017 --> 00:08:50,017
Notice anything odd?

112
00:08:50,017 --> 00:08:51,017
Huh?

113
00:08:52,017 --> 00:08:54,017
It's still moving!

114
00:08:54,017 --> 00:08:55,017
That's funny.

115
00:08:55,017 --> 00:08:58,017
I thought we had stayed here long enough for it to stabilize.

116
00:08:58,017 --> 00:08:59,017
Oh, no, you did.

117
00:08:59,017 --> 00:09:02,017
Half a day is all you need, but that's not the issue.

118
00:09:02,017 --> 00:09:08,017
For the first half of your journey, the log pose was recording the magnetic waves of each destination,

119
00:09:08,017 --> 00:09:12,017
so you were able to navigate between islands that way.

120
00:09:12,017 --> 00:09:16,017
However, the second half of the Grand Line won't be so easy to predict.

121
00:09:16,017 --> 00:09:23,017
In addition to the currents and the weather, some of the islands tend to experience changes in their magnetic waves as well.

122
00:09:23,017 --> 00:09:24,017
Huh?

123
00:09:24,017 --> 00:09:28,017
In fact, some islands have waves that disappear altogether.

124
00:09:28,017 --> 00:09:29,017
Huh?

125
00:09:29,017 --> 00:09:31,017
Then how are we supposed to find out where they are?

126
00:09:31,017 --> 00:09:34,017
Well, you're sure to lose your way with only one needle.

127
00:09:34,017 --> 00:09:38,017
But now, fortunately, you'll have three of them.

128
00:09:39,017 --> 00:09:40,017
Okay.

129
00:09:40,017 --> 00:09:43,017
So why is one of the needles moving while the other two are sitting still?

130
00:09:43,017 --> 00:09:45,017
Are you sure this thing works?

131
00:09:45,017 --> 00:09:50,017
Each of the needles is recording the magnetic waves from one of three different islands.

132
00:09:50,017 --> 00:09:57,017
This way, you'll be able to assess multiple paths and determine which way to travel based on your instincts as a navigator.

133
00:09:57,017 --> 00:10:01,017
It's likely to make the difference between life and death for you.

134
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:07,017
A skilled navigator will know which direction is safest by simply observing the slightest movement of their needles.

135
00:10:07,017 --> 00:10:12,017
There are no guarantees, but there is a good rule of thumb you can follow.

136
00:10:12,017 --> 00:10:16,017
Erratic movement means more danger.

137
00:10:16,017 --> 00:10:21,017
Changes in magnetic waves are often caused by abnormalities on the island.

138
00:10:22,017 --> 00:10:23,017
What?

139
00:10:23,017 --> 00:10:24,017
That's creepy.

140
00:10:24,017 --> 00:10:26,017
I'd rather not know that stuff, thank you.

141
00:10:26,017 --> 00:10:28,017
I'm with you on this one.

142
00:10:28,017 --> 00:10:29,017
Me too!

143
00:10:29,017 --> 00:10:31,017
Why don't you go ahead and smash that thing now?

144
00:10:31,017 --> 00:10:32,017
But you mustn't.

145
00:10:32,017 --> 00:10:35,017
Knowing where the danger is will help you travel more safely.

146
00:10:37,017 --> 00:10:38,017
Huh?

147
00:10:38,017 --> 00:10:39,017
Let me see.

148
00:10:39,017 --> 00:10:40,017
Ah!

149
00:10:40,017 --> 00:10:41,017
No!

150
00:10:41,017 --> 00:10:42,017
Luffy!

151
00:10:47,017 --> 00:10:49,017
Little one's going crazy.

152
00:10:49,017 --> 00:10:50,017
That must be where the party is.

153
00:10:50,017 --> 00:10:51,017
I say we go there.

154
00:10:53,017 --> 00:10:56,017
Oh, we're gonna die!

155
00:10:57,017 --> 00:11:00,017
Excuse me, but who's the navigator around here?

156
00:11:00,017 --> 00:11:02,017
I don't try to do your job, do I?

157
00:11:02,017 --> 00:11:03,017
So let me do mine!

158
00:11:03,017 --> 00:11:05,017
Yeah, well I'm the captain, remember?

159
00:11:05,017 --> 00:11:06,017
Uh, Captain Luffy!

160
00:11:06,017 --> 00:11:08,017
We like being alive, so please listen to her, okay?

161
00:11:08,017 --> 00:11:09,017
Don't be afraid, Nami!

162
00:11:09,017 --> 00:11:10,017
I'll protect you!

163
00:11:10,017 --> 00:11:11,017
Oh, look at her!

164
00:11:11,017 --> 00:11:12,017
She's so adorable!

165
00:11:12,017 --> 00:11:13,017
And now for the B-Side!

166
00:11:13,017 --> 00:11:14,017
I call it Wreck-Liam Boss!

167
00:11:14,017 --> 00:11:15,017
Yo!

168
00:11:15,017 --> 00:11:16,017
Are you ready?

169
00:11:16,017 --> 00:11:17,017
Cause it's time to get this show on the road, bro!

170
00:11:17,017 --> 00:11:18,017
Huh?

171
00:11:18,017 --> 00:11:21,017
Then tell me how to bring this baby back up to the top!

172
00:11:21,017 --> 00:11:22,017
Well, Luffy?

173
00:11:22,017 --> 00:11:23,017
Right!

174
00:11:23,017 --> 00:11:24,017
Let's go!

175
00:11:24,017 --> 00:11:25,017
We'll miss you!

176
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:26,017
See ya!

177
00:11:26,017 --> 00:11:27,017
No!

178
00:11:27,017 --> 00:11:28,017
No!

179
00:11:28,017 --> 00:11:29,017
No!

180
00:11:29,017 --> 00:11:30,017
No!

181
00:11:30,017 --> 00:11:31,017
No!

182
00:11:31,017 --> 00:11:32,017
No!

183
00:11:33,017 --> 00:11:34,017
I don't know how to bring this baby back up to the top!

184
00:11:34,017 --> 00:11:35,017
No!

185
00:11:35,017 --> 00:11:51,017
I'm gonna stay here and help these folks rebuild the factory.

186
00:11:51,017 --> 00:11:52,017
You sure you'll be all right without a guide?

187
00:11:52,017 --> 00:11:53,017
Sure!

188
00:11:53,017 --> 00:11:57,017
Sure, it was fun having you around, but I think we'll be okay.

189
00:11:57,017 --> 00:12:00,017
Oh sure, screw it! We don't need a guide! I mean, what's the point?

190
00:12:00,017 --> 00:12:03,017
Apparently we're just gonna waltz our way into the world of suffering and death anyway!

191
00:12:03,017 --> 00:12:07,017
Exactly! Why don't we all just die right now and save ourselves of trouble, huh?

192
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:08,017
Oh dear.

193
00:12:08,017 --> 00:12:11,017
Goodbye! Come back someday!

194
00:12:11,017 --> 00:12:16,017
He'll bet your sweet fins I will! You ladies are all I dream about!

195
00:12:16,017 --> 00:12:18,017
So much for the all blue.

196
00:12:18,017 --> 00:12:25,017
You've done so much to help our kingdom. We thank you.

197
00:12:25,017 --> 00:12:28,017
I pray that you will arrive safely.

198
00:12:28,017 --> 00:12:30,017
Thanks!

199
00:12:30,017 --> 00:12:34,017
Just you wait! By next time, whoo!

200
00:12:34,017 --> 00:12:37,017
We'll be way tougher!

201
00:12:37,017 --> 00:12:39,017
Even tougher than the great knight Neptune!

202
00:12:39,017 --> 00:12:42,017
And we'll be commanding the most powerful army under the Cephas!

203
00:12:42,017 --> 00:12:44,017
Hola tido!

204
00:12:44,017 --> 00:12:46,017
Sounds good!

205
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:54,017
Now, where's...

206
00:12:54,017 --> 00:12:58,017
There he is!

207
00:12:58,017 --> 00:13:00,017
Jinbei!

208
00:13:00,017 --> 00:13:25,217
Mr.

209
00:13:25,217 --> 00:13:31,217
All right, New World, here we come!

210
00:13:37,217 --> 00:13:40,217
It's time to set sail!

211
00:13:55,217 --> 00:14:00,217
Goodbye, Swahead!

212
00:14:05,217 --> 00:14:09,217
Well, time's a-wasting!

213
00:14:17,217 --> 00:14:20,217
Goodbye! Thank you!

214
00:14:20,217 --> 00:14:23,217
Come back with more candy and meat sometime!

215
00:14:23,217 --> 00:14:25,217
I like humans now!

216
00:14:25,217 --> 00:14:28,217
Oh, and robots and raccoons, too!

217
00:14:30,217 --> 00:14:33,217
I'm reindeer, but I'll let that one go.

218
00:14:34,217 --> 00:14:36,217
Oh, not me?

219
00:14:36,217 --> 00:14:37,217
Be careful!

220
00:14:37,217 --> 00:14:39,217
Come back any time!

221
00:14:39,217 --> 00:14:42,217
Come back for more takoyaki, okay?

222
00:14:42,217 --> 00:14:44,217
I love you!

223
00:14:44,217 --> 00:14:46,217
Every one of you!

224
00:14:48,217 --> 00:14:50,217
Ready!

225
00:14:50,217 --> 00:14:52,217
Challenge is too!

226
00:14:53,217 --> 00:14:55,217
You did remember!

227
00:14:55,217 --> 00:14:56,217
In the beginning!

228
00:14:56,217 --> 00:14:58,217
No-ho-ho-ho-ho!

229
00:14:58,217 --> 00:14:59,217
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

230
00:15:13,217 --> 00:15:14,217
Majesty!

231
00:15:14,217 --> 00:15:15,217
Don't be late!

232
00:15:15,217 --> 00:15:19,997
Help me, wait!

233
00:15:20,517 --> 00:15:21,257
Whoa!

234
00:15:22,097 --> 00:15:24,277
Shirahoshi, my love!

235
00:15:29,857 --> 00:15:31,897
I just wanted to say,

236
00:15:32,517 --> 00:15:34,577
if I get to see you again,

237
00:15:36,257 --> 00:15:38,257
then I promise you,

238
00:15:38,757 --> 00:15:40,297
I won't cry,

239
00:15:40,557 --> 00:15:42,437
at least not as much as now.

240
00:15:45,217 --> 00:15:48,157
I hope you and I can take another stroll together, Luffy.

241
00:15:48,917 --> 00:15:49,737
Oh, yeah?

242
00:15:50,317 --> 00:15:52,617
You want to go back to your mom's grave again?

243
00:15:53,697 --> 00:15:55,377
No, not this time.

244
00:15:55,897 --> 00:15:58,177
The place I want to go is farther away.

245
00:15:59,657 --> 00:16:01,957
I want to visit a real forest,

246
00:16:02,217 --> 00:16:03,217
on the surface.

247
00:16:05,117 --> 00:16:05,997
That's right.

248
00:16:06,477 --> 00:16:08,797
You've never been out of the sea before, have you?

249
00:16:10,757 --> 00:16:12,517
Sure, let's do it.

250
00:16:12,877 --> 00:16:14,957
I'll take you there first chance I get.

251
00:16:15,217 --> 00:16:15,917
Oh, yeah.

252
00:16:28,837 --> 00:16:29,677
Promise me.

253
00:16:30,957 --> 00:16:32,617
Okay, I'll thank you, Sweria.

254
00:16:33,657 --> 00:16:34,637
Leave it to me.

255
00:16:36,137 --> 00:16:37,157
Careful now, Luffy.

256
00:16:37,377 --> 00:16:39,797
If you make a promise, we have to help you keep it.

257
00:16:40,117 --> 00:16:42,217
Remember, no matter what happens,

258
00:16:42,297 --> 00:16:44,197
you must never break a promise, ever.

259
00:16:44,897 --> 00:16:46,977
You know what, though? Count me in.

260
00:16:48,797 --> 00:16:49,937
Oh, Nami!

261
00:16:50,717 --> 00:16:52,077
And me, of course.

262
00:16:52,437 --> 00:16:53,237
Yeah, me too.

263
00:16:53,717 --> 00:16:54,597
And me.

264
00:16:54,997 --> 00:16:55,757
Me too.

265
00:16:56,277 --> 00:16:57,177
Don't forget me.

266
00:16:58,297 --> 00:17:00,077
We've all given our word now.

267
00:17:00,417 --> 00:17:02,077
No bones about that.

268
00:17:06,417 --> 00:17:08,157
We won't let you down.

269
00:17:12,477 --> 00:17:13,397
Thank you.

270
00:17:15,177 --> 00:17:17,537
So don't cry anymore, okay?

271
00:17:22,257 --> 00:17:23,137
Right!

272
00:17:23,137 --> 00:17:32,137
What?

273
00:17:33,817 --> 00:17:34,017
Ha!

274
00:17:34,017 --> 00:17:34,137
Ha!

275
00:17:34,637 --> 00:17:35,217
Ha!

276
00:17:35,217 --> 00:17:35,517
Ha!

277
00:17:35,517 --> 00:17:36,037
Ha!

278
00:17:36,037 --> 00:18:06,017
I don't know.

279
00:18:06,037 --> 00:18:11,597
Never forget what they've done for us.

280
00:18:11,917 --> 00:18:12,977
We won't, Father.

281
00:18:25,397 --> 00:18:26,737
Hey, Papa!

282
00:18:28,797 --> 00:18:31,837
Can you pretty please buy me a straw hat, too?

283
00:18:32,097 --> 00:18:33,957
I want to be just like Luffy.

284
00:18:33,957 --> 00:18:38,697
I'm sorry, buddy, but they don't sell straw hats on the seafloor.

285
00:18:38,737 --> 00:18:40,437
Then go get one from up there!

286
00:18:41,057 --> 00:18:42,397
I can't do that, son.

287
00:18:42,477 --> 00:18:44,437
The surface is full of humans who hate our kind.

288
00:18:44,757 --> 00:18:46,517
There's no telling what they'll do if I...

289
00:18:46,517 --> 00:18:46,877
Huh?

290
00:18:48,257 --> 00:18:51,757
What I mean is, I've heard that some humans aren't very nice, that's all.

291
00:18:52,237 --> 00:18:53,777
But they're not all the same.

292
00:18:53,957 --> 00:18:55,637
Some of them are heroes, like Straw Hat Luffy.

293
00:18:55,637 --> 00:19:02,917
Hey, Boss Jinbei! Perfect timing!

294
00:19:04,777 --> 00:19:06,377
I just overheard.

295
00:19:07,117 --> 00:19:11,617
I'm going to ask a merchant to get his hands on some of those straw hats for us.

296
00:19:11,797 --> 00:19:12,277
Really?

297
00:19:12,277 --> 00:19:13,977
Yes, my boy.

298
00:19:14,677 --> 00:19:17,037
You'd like to be a hero, wouldn't you?

299
00:19:17,757 --> 00:19:18,277
Uh-huh!

300
00:19:18,277 --> 00:19:44,217
I miss it already!

301
00:19:44,797 --> 00:19:46,797
All those gorgeous mermaids!

302
00:19:47,897 --> 00:19:49,317
Look alive, you guys!

303
00:19:49,457 --> 00:19:50,337
Don't goof off!

304
00:19:50,837 --> 00:19:53,577
Once we ascend, who knows what trouble we might run into.

305
00:19:54,357 --> 00:19:56,937
You remember how scary it was on the way down, don't you?

306
00:20:02,557 --> 00:20:03,077
Huh?

307
00:20:03,377 --> 00:20:05,057
What's with the weird boxes, Frankie?

308
00:20:05,517 --> 00:20:07,857
Those are hollow cubes made out of banyan.

309
00:20:08,257 --> 00:20:09,457
They're going to help us float.

310
00:20:09,457 --> 00:20:14,397
I can even adjust the ship's speed based on how many I throw!

311
00:20:17,937 --> 00:20:18,297
Huh?

312
00:20:19,037 --> 00:20:19,477
Luffy!

313
00:20:19,917 --> 00:20:20,597
What's up?

314
00:20:29,097 --> 00:20:31,037
Once we reach the new world...

315
00:20:33,037 --> 00:20:35,717
...Shanks won't be far away.

316
00:20:39,457 --> 00:20:43,357
I hope I see him soon.

317
00:20:44,457 --> 00:20:48,217
In that case, I'll leave this hat to you.

318
00:20:49,337 --> 00:20:51,697
It means more to me than anything else.

319
00:20:52,457 --> 00:20:54,457
I want you to bring this hat back to me.

320
00:20:54,937 --> 00:20:57,217
But not until you've become a great pirate.

321
00:20:57,217 --> 00:21:03,897
There is one thing...

322
00:21:03,897 --> 00:21:05,797
...that hurts.

323
00:21:07,117 --> 00:21:09,217
I won't be around...

324
00:21:09,217 --> 00:21:11,897
...to see you fulfill your dream.

325
00:21:12,557 --> 00:21:13,297
That's fine.

326
00:21:13,877 --> 00:21:14,717
I have faith.

327
00:21:15,297 --> 00:21:16,417
You can do it.

328
00:21:16,417 --> 00:21:19,517
Because you're my brother.

329
00:21:20,637 --> 00:21:22,797
There is yet joy beyond your sorrows.

330
00:21:23,637 --> 00:21:24,997
What's gone may be gone.

331
00:21:25,597 --> 00:21:29,517
But you still have something left in this world to treasure, don't you?

332
00:21:29,937 --> 00:21:32,357
Let nothing stop you from reaching the top.

333
00:21:33,157 --> 00:21:38,697
By the way, I was wondering if you've ever heard the name they use for the second half of the Grand Line.

334
00:21:38,697 --> 00:21:48,417
On the other side of the Red Line, at the far reaches of the ocean, is a place that few pirates or marines have ever seen.

335
00:21:48,957 --> 00:21:49,697
They call it...

336
00:21:50,497 --> 00:21:51,677
The New World.

337
00:21:53,257 --> 00:21:54,497
The New World!

338
00:21:54,497 --> 00:21:59,657
There's a new era coming.

339
00:22:00,077 --> 00:22:02,897
And the people who can guide it are gathering on those seas.

340
00:22:03,537 --> 00:22:07,817
They say the one who can master those waters will become king of the pilots.

341
00:22:10,477 --> 00:22:13,037
Who knows what's waiting for us up there?

342
00:22:14,637 --> 00:22:16,657
That's the greatest sea in the world!

343
00:22:17,217 --> 00:22:18,197
Took long enough.

344
00:22:18,777 --> 00:22:20,057
I'm ready for some action.

345
00:22:20,257 --> 00:22:21,937
It won't be long now, Laboon.

346
00:22:22,217 --> 00:22:23,777
Just one half to go.

347
00:22:23,777 --> 00:22:26,177
With this new log pose, I can take us anywhere.

348
00:22:26,657 --> 00:22:29,037
And wherever we go, the sunning can handle it.

349
00:22:29,257 --> 00:22:31,237
Don't worry, I'll treat all your injuries!

350
00:22:31,957 --> 00:22:34,397
And as long as I'm around, you'll never go hungry.

351
00:22:34,917 --> 00:22:36,857
The great Usopp's got your back too!

352
00:22:42,857 --> 00:22:43,617
Alright!

353
00:22:45,857 --> 00:22:46,937
Let's go!

354
00:22:53,777 --> 00:23:10,997
The Straw Hats depart from Fishman Island and ascend to the surface.

355
00:23:10,997 --> 00:23:16,437
The journey is not a short one, however, and it is filled with sea monsters of increasingly massive size.

356
00:23:16,917 --> 00:23:22,237
While Luffy tries to make dinner out of the underwater abominations, the Sunny encounters a deadly whirlpool.

357
00:23:22,717 --> 00:23:26,817
Helpless against its whipping waters, the crew must hope for a miracle to survive.

358
00:23:26,817 --> 00:23:34,237
On the next One Piece, to the new world, heading for the ultimate sea, I'm going to be king of the pirates!

359
00:23:34,237 --> 00:23:51,437
The

